{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 19, :comments ["Do not marvel that a term of death is said of the land, for the opposite is <b>ואתה מחיה את כולם</b> (Nehemiah 9:6)." "<b>תשם.</b> From the root of <b>והבמות תישמנה</b> (Ezekiel 6:6), and its pattern you will know. We find in the derash that the famine departed in the merit of Jacob, and it is possible that the famine was three years, and was not like the four that passed."], :book :genesis, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"] ["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:48:12.346578316Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}